1. manage.py: A command-line utility used to perform administrative tasks in a Django project.

2. settings.py: Contains all the main configuration and settings of the Django project.

3. urls.py: Defines the URL routes and maps URLs to the appropriate views.

4. wsgi.py: Acts as an entry point for running and deploying Django applications using WSGI servers.

5. asgi.py: Acts as an entry point for running and deploying Django applications using ASGI servers, including asynchronous applications.